{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. You’re here because of nausea and vomiting again, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been vomiting all day. I tried the Zofran I have at home, but it didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And your blood sugars—how have they been?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They’ve been in the 150s to 200s. I took my Lantus last night at 10, like usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good. No signs of diabetic ketoacidosis, which is reassuring. Did you eat anything this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I tried some toast and soda, but I threw it all up. Then my back pain got worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any abdominal pain, diarrhea, or other symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:04:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no belly pain or anything like that. Just the nausea, vomiting, and now my back is really bothering me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. In the ER, you got some IV Zofran, ketorolac, and Dilaudid. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. The nausea is calmer, but my back still aches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep managing that. Your labs look stable—no infection, kidneys are okay, and your electrolytes are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried about my sugars or kidneys again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching closely. Since you have type 1 diabetes, we want to avoid both high and low sugars. You had one mild low this morning, but you treated it with food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, around 6 AM. I had some juice and it came back up. But I ate a cracker after that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good job catching that. We’ll keep your insulin the same as before—no changes to your Lantus or Novolog."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I don’t want to go too low again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Now, about the nausea—since Zofran ODT isn’t helping at home, we’re suggesting you try Ativan next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ativan? Like for anxiety? But I’m not anxious when I’m nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can help with nausea too, especially in people with diabetes. It works on the brain’s nausea center. And since you already take lorazepam, it’s safe to try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So instead of Zofran, take Ativan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 1 mg. We’re updating your prescription so you can try it next time symptoms start."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2125-06-15 15:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll give it a shot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’ve been doing well—no vomiting since this morning, and you sipped some broth without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel much better. Still a little queasy, but not throwing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to advance your diet to a regular diabetic meal tomorrow. If you keep this up, you could go home tomorrow afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What about my back pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting you on gabapentin—200 mg three times a day. It’s for nerve-related pain and might help more than tizanidine did."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t keep taking tizanidine—it didn’t help. But I liked the lidocaine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. But insurance requires a trial of gabapentin first. If this doesn’t work, we can apply for the patches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So I have to try this first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And you can increase the dose slowly—by 200 mg each week, up to 400 mg three times a day, if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So start at 200, then go up if it’s not helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. But don’t go over 1200 mg a day unless we say so."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I can still use the menthol cream and acetaminophen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2125-06-15 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both are fine. Use them as needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did great overnight—no vomiting, ate breakfast without issues, and your sugars are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Ready to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you today. Keep taking the gabapentin daily, even if your back feels okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if it doesn’t help, I can call about the lidocaine patches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Also, try Ativan next time nausea starts. And keep following up with your new care team, especially the Chronic Pain Service."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for helping me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2125-06-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you only if you really need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2125-06-15 14:48:00",
    "admission_end": "2125-06-16 14:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and chronic back pain was admitted for recurrent nausea and vomiting. She had tried Zofran at home without success and presented with worsening symptoms and back pain. IV antiemetics provided relief, and she tolerated advancement to a regular diabetic diet. Her blood glucose remained stable except for one episode of mild hypoglycemia, managed with food. The insulin regimen was unchanged. Gabapentin was started for back pain as a required trial before lidocaine patch approval. She was advised to use Ativan instead of Zofran for future nausea episodes. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up planned with her new care team, including the Chronic Pain Service.",
    "problems": [
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Backache, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with unspecified complication, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
